# DEPRECATED since 0.3.5, and no longer served by fusioncore_node.
#
# This type is kept only so that packages built against 0.3.4 or earlier still
# compile. Nothing advertises it. Use robot_localization/srv/FromLL instead:
#
#   ros2 service call /fromLL robot_localization/srv/FromLL
#     "{ll_point: {latitude: 43.2589, longitude: -79.9132, altitude: 0.0}}"
#
# Why the switch: having identical fields is not enough. ROS 2 matches services
# on name AND type, so nav2_waypoint_follower (which hardcodes the
# robot_localization type) never saw the service it was waiting for and hung with
# no error. Matching the field layout but not the type name made the /fromLL
# service unusable by the one client that needed it. See issue #73.
#
# Convert GPS lat/lon/alt to map frame x/y/z. Returns the point in the local ENU
# frame anchored at the first GPS fix (or the configured reference.x/y/z origin).
# Returns zeros if the GPS reference has not been set yet (no fix received since
# node start or last reset).
geographic_msgs/GeoPoint ll_point
---
geometry_msgs/Point map_point
